WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.000
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.430
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.140
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.140
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:44.660
I understand now that Chaos Control caused a warp in time and space and that's why you were all flown over into this world.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:50.170
But what is the Chaos Emerald that caused that Chaos Control?

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:55.340
The Chaos Emerald is the Chaos Emerald and nothing else.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:02:02.140
There's a legend that says if you gather all seven Chaos Emeralds, the entire world will be yours.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.270
But it didn't work out that way.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.810
Legend ended as legend.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.150
Did it end?

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:16.780
I guess it's ended the moment the Chaos Emeralds disappeared.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.360
They haven't disappeared.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:27.370
After the seven Chaos Emeralds are brought together, they scatter all over again.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:30.370
Which means they are still somewhere?

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:32.080
That's right.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:41.180
But we don't know where they've scattered to; our home world or this world here.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:49.480
If they are somewhere in this world, if we search and find all seven Emeralds and cause Chaos Control once again,

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:53.860
you can all go back to where you came from. Right, Sonic?

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.650
Well, I guess so!

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:01.590
Episode 4

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:01.590
Get The Chaos Emerald!

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:30.640
President, we've found them.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.230
What? Where are they?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.190
The animals are at the house of a distinguished family in Station Square,

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:42.030
and Dr. Eggman is on a nameless island in the Southern Sea.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.160
Okay, capture them!

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:45.450
Right this minute.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:50.540
Please wait! It'd be better to gather all the information before we make any moves.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:56.630
Then hurry and find out the identity of this terrorist, Dr. Eggman!

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:03.220
We have already dispatched a reconnaissance team to the Southern Sea to watch over him.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.000
And what about the animals?

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:42.670
We've already started watching over them, but we are planning to dispatch another agent over to the house.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:58.520
Yeah, it was unreal! At first, I thought that some movie had begun!

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:02.190
Me too! Hey Chris, you saw the news too, didn't you?

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:04.990
...Yep.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:17.670
I have news for all of you. Your homeroom teacher, Wendy quit yesterday

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:23.630
in order to participate in the International Super Quiz.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.670
What?!

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:31.760
Therefore Mr. Stewart here will be your teacher starting today.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.680
Nice to meet you.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.230
Nice to meet you too!

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.750
Danny, are you ready?

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.580
I'll be right there!

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:12.510
Christopher Thorndyke, your father is Nelson Thorndyke the CEO of Starship Software,

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:17.430
who holds 70% of the shares of the computer world. Your mother is movie star Lindsey Fair.

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:20.810
Any problems?

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:28.450
No. The thing is I've been your mother's fan for a long time!

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.160
Oh, I see.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:33.330
Nice to meet you, Chris.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:35.740
Nice to meet you too!

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:40.500
By the way, what kind of animals do you like, Chris?

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:46.050
Uh... Hedgehogs, I guess.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.010
Oh!

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.010
Strange?

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:50.970
No, not at all.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.140
Chris!

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:56.810
Chris, thanks for waiting!

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:58.680
Goodbye then, Mr. Stewart.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.020
You're late! Let's hurry! Sorry!

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.500
What? Yikes!

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.880
Stop! I tell you.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:31.680
Stop, I said!

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.450
It's coming this way!

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.740
Look out! Get out of the way!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.420
What happened?

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.300
Well I don't have the slightest idea either.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:34.410
Hey Chris, what were you talking to Mr. Stewart about yesterday?

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:38.160
He asked me what my favorite animal is and stuff like that.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.200
What's up with that?

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:44.210
A strange stone was found at the construction site of a West Jingle department store.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:51.670
It appears to be a gem stone, but it made machines gauges go haywire when nearby.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:57.970
Perhaps all you viewers are already seeing the effects of this stone on the images of your TV screen.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:05.980
You may see or hear static. These are caused by the energy that is emitted by the stone.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.700
This is what the stone looks like.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:23.160
We've got to tell Sonic about it.

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:32.050
Now, what shall I do?

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:34.260
Big trouble, Sonic!

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:34.970
What's up?

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:38.590
Big trouble, big trouble!

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:44.560
There's been no sign of radioactivity detected within several kilometers of testing.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:50.190
Scientists are baffled as to why this stone makes machines go haywire.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:54.860
This was Scarlett Garcia, SSTV.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:02.490
It's the Chaos Emerald! So it was here in this world!

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.080
Hey!

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.330
I shuffled the cards really good!

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.790
Now, let me see.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.420
Which should I choose today?

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.090
This one!

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:19.550
Pulling the lever!

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.930
Bingo!

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.930
This is the one!

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.590
The terrorists are making their move.

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:58.340
Roger!

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:10.520
If I get a hold of the Chaos Emerald, I can create an even stronger robot. And with a stronger robot, Sonic would be a piece of cake!

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:39.630
Tails, please be careful.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.550
Yes, I know.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:46.260
Sonic left saying he was going ahead of us, but does he know where to go?

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:49.890
I guess so, because he knew last time too, didn't he?

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.690
Last time it was in a conspicuous place in town.

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:55.560
But I wonder where it's going to be this time.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.070
I don't see it anywhere.

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:08.450
I guess I'll wait for Tails and the others to come.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:18.090
From up here, I'll see when they arrive.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:33.890
Who's that coming after me?

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:41.820
This is fun. Play to your heart's content, E-11!!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:13:04.300
Oh, come on. I thought I could have more fun, but how disappointing.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:12.310
Therefore... what is the answer?

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.610
What's the matter, Chris?

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:26.910
No it's nothing. Mr. Stewart! I just remembered that I had something very important to attend to!

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.660
Hey, Chris!

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:33.870
Quiet, everyone! I just remembered I have something to do too.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.710
So please study on your own for a while.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:41.250
What? But you have to teach!

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:52.510
West Jingle Street. Okay then.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.700
So they've finally come!

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.450
I was just about tired of waiting.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:15.250
Sonic!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.410
Over there!

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.370
I guess this way is faster.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.310
I'll put two hundred on the Holidays.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.930
Are you serious? No matter you think about it, the Snakes are gonna win.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:38.890
Especially since their best player is doing great!

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:39.940
Huh?

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:41.860
Huh, what's up?

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:43.940
Well, that…

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:45.690
What?

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:52.530
Oh! It's Dr. Eggman!

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.300
I wonder what's going on?

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:21.650
I see. So, Dr. Eggman's come to get the Chaos Emerald too.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.030
So there it is.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:47.000
So it's him again. E-11, let's get the Chaos Emerald later.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.300
Get rid of Sonic first!

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:17.740
What!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.590
I'm not a ball.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:32.630
Amy, give Sonic the ring!

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:36.390
Sonic, catch this.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:39.930
Here goes!

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:44.270
All right!

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.400
No way!

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:51.820
Amy...

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.280
Ah. I messed up.

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.320
Hey, can you get any closer?

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.660
It's tough, but I'll give it a try.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:11.630
Serves you right. In the meantime, I'm going to go get the Chaos Emerald!

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:30.320
Who are you?!

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:33.440
So this is the Chaos Emerald!

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:43.950
You thief!

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:49.500
What? How rude. How dare you call Dr. Eggman a thief.

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:52.250
Give it back!

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:52.840
No.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.420
Give it back!

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.010
Get out of the way!

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:56.840
Give it back!

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:11.900
Quit it!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.000
Sonic!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:29.620
Here!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:30.710
Okay!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.400
Help!

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:56.440
Chris!

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:02.950
Chris!

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.660
Chris!

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:45.830
Ouch, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:48.120
Hey, let go! Let go!

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.250
No! I don't want to!

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:51.830
Let go, I said!

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.750
No way!

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:00.970
How dare he pull on my mustache. He pulled some hairs out.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:03.260
The Emerald!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:23.910
Please make it in time.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.190
Oops, I have no time to be rest.

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:57.860
I've got to go back to school.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.870
Look! Look! It's the Chaos Emerald!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:15.500
We've got one for a start!

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.210
We've got six more to go!

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:21.710
But we can't keep it here because it'll make the machines go haywire.

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:25.590
No problem. I'll adjust the machines for you.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:28.390
Really, well thanks.

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:30.310
You're welcome.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.940
Uh… I'm sorry.

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:41.480
Why are you apologizing?

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.940
For making you worry...

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:47.240
No problem. Hey, Chris...

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:51.740
You were really cool!

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:56.750
Really?

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:01.880
But don't get too reckless, because you're not Sonic.

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:06.880
Right!

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:48.840
<b>Tabidatsu junbi wa dekita kai?</b>

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:48.840
<i>Are you ready to go on a journey?</i>

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:52.100
<b>mata hitotsu asa ga kuru</b>

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:52.100
<i>Another morning has arrived</i>

00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:55.600
<b>Atarashii shatsu ni kigaete</b>

00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:55.600
<i>Change into a new shirt</i>

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:59.080
<b>Kurayami wo nukedasou</b>

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:59.080
<i>And escape the darkness</i>

00:22:59.080 --> 00:23:02.520
<b>Nemuranai machi wa kyou mo</b>

00:22:59.080 --> 00:23:06.690
<i>The sleepless city quietly watches over you again today</i>

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:06.690
<b>Shizuka ni tada mimamotteiru</b>

00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:12.760
<b>Kimi to boku ga hajimatteyuku!</b>

00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:12.760
<i>We begin to go!</i>

00:23:12.760 --> 00:23:16.330
<b>To be shine, To be free</b>

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:19.040
<b>Tomadowanai de</b>

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:19.040
<i>Don't be bewildered</i>

00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:25.960
<b>Toki no nami wa tsuyoku yasashii</b>

00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:25.960
<i>The waves of time are strong and kind</i>

00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:31.010
<b>Sugu ni sugu ni kimi wo mukae ni yuku</b>

00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:31.010
<i>I will come quickly to meet you</i>

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:37.140
<b>Kimi to boku no sekai wo terasou</b>

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:37.140
<i>Shine a light on our world</i>

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:40.640
<b>To be shine, To be free</b>

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:44.150
<b>Kowagaranai de</b>

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:44.150
<i>Don't be scared</i>

00:23:44.150 --> 00:23:50.320
<b>Toki no nami wa tsuyoku yasashii</b>

00:23:44.150 --> 00:23:50.320
<i>The waves of time are strong and kind</i>

00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:54.740
<b>Haruka tooi michi no mukou gawa e</b>

00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:54.740
<i>At the other end of the very long road</i>

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:58.200
<b>Sugu ni sugu ni kimi wo mukae ni yuku</b>

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:58.200
<i>I will come quickly to meet you</i>

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:02.330
<b>Kimi to boku no mirai mitsukeyou ze</b>

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:02.330
<i>Let's find our future</i>

00:24:30.010 --> 00:25:35.360
Clash!! Sonic vs Knuckles
